            <ArticleTitle>Prion-like Domains Program Ewing's Sarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0092-8674(17)31059-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cell.2017.09.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prion-like domains have emerged as important drivers of neurodegenerative disease. Now, Boulay et al. establish that the translocated prion-like domain of the oncogenic EWS-FLI1 fusion protein enables phase-separation events, which inappropriately recruit chromatin-remodeling factors to elicit the aberrant transcriptional programs underlying Ewing's sarcoma.</AbstractText>
